./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000089-20260519-054228.log:1202:- Schema changes are versioned SQL files under internal/controlplane/store/migrate/migrations/ named NNNN_name.up.sql (required) + NNNN_name.down.sql (optional, reversible-only), embedded via //go:embed. The migrate.Migrator runner owns a checksummed schema_migrations ledger, serialises with a pg advisory lock, and runs each migration in its own transaction. Migrator.Up is idempotent and refuses dirty / unknown-version / checksum-mismatch databases (errors.Is sentinels ErrDirtyDatabase/ErrUnknownVersion/ErrChecksumMismatch). NEVER edit an applied migration file (trips ErrChecksumMismatch by design) — add a new higher-versioned migration. Persistence tests are integration tests: they connect via YALLA_TEST_DATABASE_URL, create an isolated throwaway database per test, and t.Skip when the env var is unset so go test ./... stays green without Postgres. docker-compose.yml at repo root provisions local Postgres. pgx (github.com/jackc/pgx/v5 + pgxpool) is the Postgres driver.
./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000089-20260519-054228.log:1203:- Persistence tests use the shared harness internal/controlplane/testutil: RequireDB(t) gives an empty isolated throwaway Postgres database per test, RequireMigratedDB(t) also applies migrations; both t.Skip with testutil.SkipReason when YALLA_TEST_DATABASE_URL is unset and drop the DB on cleanup (parallel-safe — unique DB name per call). testutil.NewFactory(t) builds deterministic, globally-unique in-memory fixtures for the Organization->Project->Environment->Service hierarchy + User/APIKey (two factories never collide). testutil.AssertRedacted/AssertRedactedValue guard "must not leak a secret" assertions. store/migrate keeps its own local testPool — it cannot import testutil (import cycle: testutil imports migrate). Keep pure decision logic (lookupAdminDSN, scanLeaks) unexported + white-box tested, since testing.TB is sealed and cannot be faked.
./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000089-20260519-054228.log:1206:- Domain tables live in versioned migrations under store/migrate/migrations/. Every customer-data table carries organization_id (directly or via a verified parent chain) and is tenant-isolated at the database level by COMPOSITE foreign keys: a child FK (organization_id, parent_id) references the parent's UNIQUE (organization_id, id), making a cross-tenant child unrepresentable. Slugs are citext, unique within parent scope, never global. users is a global identity table; org membership is the memberships join table. Schema-level integration tests live in package store_test (NOT package migrate — it can't import testutil) and match constraint violations via *pgconn.PgError SQLSTATE class 23.
