./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000101-20260519-072132.log:708:- Verification-suite single-file multi-surface static-test, migrations-from-empty-DB instance (BE-0389 pattern, internal/release/verification_suite_migrations_empty_db_static_test.go + internal/controlplane/store/migrate/migrate_test.go's new canonical pair TestMigrationsEmptyDBContractCoversAllNumberedFiles + TestMigrationsEmptyDBContractAppliesEmbeddedLadderToEmptyDatabase + SECURITY.md "## Migration Tests From Empty DB" section AND a new row in the Required Verification Gates table + internal/release/AGENTS.md "## Verification suite: migration tests from empty DB (BE-0389)" subsection; ELEVENTH worked instance of the BE-0379..BE-0388 verification-suite mega-pattern, canonical command `go test -run TestMigrationsEmptyDB ./...`, CI step name `Migration tests from empty DB`, verify.sh prefix #15). Four BE-0389-specific extensions to the template: (1) `CANONICAL PAIR ENCODES DETERMINISTIC × POSTGRES-REQUIRED DUAL` — unlike every prior verification-suite story whose canonical pair pinned two invariants on the same execution substrate, BE-0389's pair splits across two SUBSTRATES: TestMigrationsEmptyDBContractCoversAllNumberedFiles runs on the embed.FS alone (no Postgres dependency, runs on every developer machine and every CI runner deterministically); TestMigrationsEmptyDBContractAppliesEmbeddedLadderToEmptyDatabase requires a real Postgres (creates a throwaway database via crypto/rand-named DSN, runs the embedded ladder, asserts schema_migrations is clean, skips with t.Skip when YALLA_TEST_DATABASE_URL is unset). The deterministic member is the FRONT LINE — it trips on every machine on any closed-set coverage regression (new NNNN_*.up.sql file the loader misses, numbered file renamed to non-numbered form, version gap). The Postgres member is the DEPTH gate — it asserts the runtime contract that no migration can fail on an empty DB. Forward-applicable to ANY future verification story whose contract spans de