./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000019-20260518-211930.log:857:- Schema changes are versioned SQL files under internal/controlplane/store/migrate/migrations/ named NNNN_name.up.sql (required) + NNNN_name.down.sql (optional, reversible-only), embedded via //go:embed. The migrate.Migrator runner owns a checksummed schema_migrations ledger, serialises with a pg advisory lock, and runs each migration in its own transaction. Migrator.Up is idempotent and refuses dirty / unknown-version / checksum-mismatch databases (errors.Is sentinels ErrDirtyDatabase/ErrUnknownVersion/ErrChecksumMismatch). NEVER edit an applied migration file (trips ErrChecksumMismatch by design) — add a new higher-versioned migration. Persistence tests are integration tests: they connect via YALLA_TEST_DATABASE_URL, create an isolated throwaway database per test, and t.Skip when the env var is unset so go test ./... stays green without Postgres. docker-compose.yml at repo root provisions local Postgres. pgx (github.com/jackc/pgx/v5 + pgxpool) is the Postgres driver.
./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000019-20260518-211930.log:858:- Persistence tests use the shared harness internal/controlplane/testutil: RequireDB(t) gives an empty isolated throwaway Postgres database per test, RequireMigratedDB(t) also applies migrations; both t.Skip with testutil.SkipReason when YALLA_TEST_DATABASE_URL is unset and drop the DB on cleanup (parallel-safe — unique DB name per call). testutil.NewFactory(t) builds deterministic, globally-unique in-memory fixtures for the Organization->Project->Environment->Service hierarchy + User/APIKey (two factories never collide). testutil.AssertRedacted/AssertRedactedValue guard "must not leak a secret" assertions. store/migrate keeps its own local testPool — it cannot import testutil (import cycle: testutil imports migrate). Keep pure decision logic (lookupAdminDSN, scanLeaks) unexported + white-box tested, since testing.TB is sealed and cannot be faked.
./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000019-20260518-211930.log:861:- Domain tables live in versioned migrations under store/migrate/migrations/. Every customer-data table carries organization_id (directly or via a verified parent chain) and is tenant-isolated at the database level by COMPOSITE foreign keys: a child FK (organization_id, parent_id) references the parent's UNIQUE (organization_id, id), making a cross-tenant child unrepresentable. Slugs are citext, unique within parent scope, never global. users is a global identity table; org membership is the memberships join table. Schema-level integration tests live in package store_test (NOT package migrate — it can't import testutil) and match constraint violations via *pgconn.PgError SQLSTATE class 23.
./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000019-20260518-211930.log:905:- Pagination contract package (BE-0037, internal/controlplane/pagination): every customer-facing list endpoint composes the shared pagination.Params + pagination.Cursor + pagination.Page[T] envelope rather than reimplementing limit/cursor/sort/filter parsing. ParseParams(url.Values, ParseOptions) parses ?limit= ?cursor= ?sort= ?direction= ?filter.<k>= with stable apierr.InvalidInput (E_INVALID_INPUT) violations whose Reason text NEVER echoes the submitted value (only classification + accepted range — protects against reflection-style content channels), accumulates multiple violations into one envelope, enforces the package MaxLimit=200 ceiling even when an endpoint misconfigures its own, and rejects a cursor whose embedded Sort/Direction disagrees with the request as a stable 400 "fetch the first page again" instead of silently serving overlapping pages. Cursor is base64url-encoded JSON {v: "yalla.cursor.v1", p: Position, s: Sort, d: Direction} — opaque to clients, deterministic (same input -> same encoding so HTTP fixtures diff byte-for-byte), URL-safe (RawURLEncoding, no '+/='), and DOES NOT carry an organization_id / tenant / principal field by contract (a TestDecodeCursorTenantIsolationCannotBeBypassed test guards this so adding one is impossible without breaking the suite — tenant isolation stays the persistence layer's responsibility, cursor only encodes a within-set position). Page[T any] is the wire shape: Items always non-nil (BuildPage guarantees []T{} for empty), NextCursor omitempty (empty string == end of stream — agents do NOT compare len(Items) to limit), TotalEstimate *int64 omitempty (nil = "not cheap to compute", endpoints must NOT fabricate a value). BuildPage uses the over-fetch strategy: store fetches Limit+1 rows, BuildPage trims to Limit and encodes next_cursor from the last retained row's position via a PositionFunc[T] adapter. Cursor stability under inserts is proven end-to-end by