./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000120-20260519-101059.log:705:- Verification-suite single-file multi-surface static-test, port-driven-pure-classifier instance (BE-0406 pattern, internal/release/verification_suite_import_dry_run_static_test.go + internal/controlplane/migrateimport/import_dry_run_canonical_test.go's new canonical pair TestImportDryRunCoversCallSites + TestImportDryRunPreservesContractUnderContention + SECURITY.md "## Import Dry-Run Tests" section AND a new row in the Required Verification Gates table + internal/release/AGENTS.md "## Verification suite: import dry-run tests (BE-0406)" subsection; TWENTY-EIGHTH worked instance of the BE-0379..BE-0405 verification-suite mega-pattern. Canonical command `go test -run TestImportDryRun ./...`, CI step name `Import dry-run tests`, verify.sh prefix #30 inserted between BE-0405's #29 and the trailing optionals renumbered #30-#34 → #31-#35 in the same edit (with the BE-0400 external-smoke static-test constants `# 34 → # 35` and synthetic-fixture `# 33 → # 34` updated to match). Three forward-applicable extensions specific to the FIRST port-driven-pure-classifier instance — the chokepoint is `(*migrateimport.Importer).Plan(ctx, PlanInput) (Plan, error)` which is deterministic but reads from port interfaces (Scanner, Repository) rather than being a package-level pure function: (1) `THE CONTENTION BURST BUILDS A FRESH IMPORTER PER ITERATION — NOT A SHARED INSTANCE — BECAUSE THE CHOKEPOINT TAKES PORT INTERFACES AT CONSTRUCTION TIME` — unlike BE-0405 (which has no shared receiver because Diff is a package-level function), the import-dry-run chokepoint is a method on Importer whose fake Scanner/Repository are scenario-specific. Each goroutine therefore builds its own (Snapshot, fake Repository, Importer) triple per iteration. The burst's value shifts from "package has no shared state" to "the planner's internal pure logic (classify, pendingOwnerItems, proposeSlug, indexProjectsByID, indexEnvironmentsByID, indexService